answers.body:
@sunny-g haha, that was my typo. I’ve fixed it and rebased onto the latest commit.

By the way, you can simply copy it into your config, just like I did in [my config](https://github.com/yzx9/nix-config/tree/main/homeManagerModules/hermes-agent). This way, you can stay aligned with the mainline branch.

It’s been working well on my side. The only issue I’ve run into is a minor bug with secret management: if you update your secrets, you may need to manually edit `~/.local/share/hermes/.hermes/.env`. I’ll address this properly once #10139 is merged.

